WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:06.800
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, yesterday I
asked you all to submit Game of Thrones questions

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:11.349
so today we’ll see what everyone has to
say about what’s really going with the gods.

00:00:11.349 --> 00:00:18.189
I always like the what would you be if you
were in the story questions.

00:00:18.189 --> 00:00:22.740
I’ll announce who won the book after we
get through everything, if you are just finding

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.269
me the book giveaway happens every week when
I post my bonus videos. The next one starts

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:29.369
next week so be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:32.820
General spoilers for everything through season
4 I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:37.210
Question 1 - Shadow Wolf asks do dragons have
gods?

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:43.100
The dragons are more like animals. Like really
intuitive flying lizards. I think they just

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.960
operate on primal instinct. But they are connected
to the balance of nature in a way that hasn’t

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.239
been fully explained.

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:50.899
It’s more likely that people would have
worshipped them prior to the valyrians learning

00:00:50.899 --> 00:00:55.730
how to domesticate them. In a sense they’re
a lot like horses to the Dothraki. They are

00:00:55.730 --> 00:00:58.149
a part of the culture and highly respected.

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:03.359
You could argue that they serve nature or
the old gods, but worshiping a god and serving

00:01:03.359 --> 00:01:05.519
one are two different things.

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:09.460
I think Dragons are connected to fire magic,
R’hollor is presented as the Lord of Light.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.180
So you could link them to him too.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.530
Then there are the Daenerys Azor Ahai theories.
Which I think I’ve talked about in my other

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:18.130
theory videos. So if you had to pick I would
say they exist on the side Red God or The

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.259
Old Gods, but I don’t think it’s going
to be that simple.

00:01:20.259 --> 00:01:25.229
Just to explain how they’re connected to
fire magic it’s really the seasons. Back

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:29.310
when dragons started to proliferate more the
world started to get hotter. So the summer

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:32.409
season became much longer, then after the
last dragon died the world started to cool

00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:33.909
again. That was in the years preceding the
show. Thus Winter is Coming.

00:01:33.909 --> 00:01:37.340
Thus, Dragons have a certain connection to
the balance of seasons.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:42.119
Question 2 - Rainbow fish bubbles asks Do
out think that the children might someday

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:46.310
serve the great other? Or will the children
make the white walkers bow down to them and

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.469
their gods?

00:01:48.469 --> 00:01:53.119
The Children were involved in stopping the
forces of the great other at the end of the

00:01:53.119 --> 00:02:00.119
Long Night. It’s implied that a peace treaty
was brokered and they were involved in sealing

00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:02.420
that pact.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:06.070
I think they’re more of a neutral force
serving nature. They want balance, so if one

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.310
side got too powerful, they would probably
work with the other side to create balance.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:17.160
There is a theory that the three eyed raven
will be a champion of the great other, but

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:24.160
that doesn’t mean that he’s evil. And
if Priests of the Red God can disagree then

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.250
so can greenseers. The three eyed raven was
the last greenseer until bran came to learn

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.110
from him.

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:35.550
So even if the children work on the opposing
side of the red god, it doesn’t mean they

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.000
are surrendering or bowing down. It would
probably only be in service of the natural

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.020
order of things.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.600
For instance, if Dragons can make the world
hotter, and they started to overpopulate,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.750
the world would turn into one giant desert.
So the forces of cold or night or however

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.880
you want to think about it would have to suppress
them until the world returned to a more balanced

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.210
Question 3 - Ablix asks Who did the Valyrians
worship?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:57.800
They worshiped a wide variety of dieties,
there wasn’t a main religion. The Valyrian

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.910
freehold was created after the Valyrians tamed
dragons and used them to conquer the eastern

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:02.420
continent.

00:03:02.420 --> 00:03:06.440
So just like Greeks or the Romans, you ended
up with a wide variety of citizens from conquered

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.570
nations all with their own gods.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:11.910
Beyond that we don’t know if the Valyrians
worshipped any specific deity before they

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:17.090
tamed dragons. Because they lived in this
area near slaver’s bay and the summer sea

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:21.310
you can point to precursors of a lot of the
different gods people worship in Mereen.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:25.200
I’m not an expert on the evolution of religions
in the world. Most early religion was just

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:30.040
tied to burial rites. Like the way the religion
of the Old gods doesn’t have a lot of complex

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.050
customs.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.970
George RR Martin has teased that he’ll write
flashbacks to old valyria before the doom.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.230
So be sure to read winds of winter and dream
of spring when they come out.

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:40.880
So far, the only people in the series that
have claimed to actually travel there is Euron

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:44.340
Greyjoy and it seems like the show isn’t
going to do his character.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:48.730
Tywin Lannister’s youngest brother Gerion
Lannister traveled to Valyria to try and recover

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:53.460
Brighroar, the lost Valyrian blade of House
Lannister. But he never returned. He’s kind

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.420
of interesting in that he wasn’t a huge
fan of Tywin and tried to help Tyrion learn

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.270
history as a child.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.650
I don’t think the show is going to do that
character, but Tyrion might run into him again

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.470
in the books in the east.

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:07.080
Question 4 - Edward Faull asks What do you
think is going to happen at the end of the

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.880
series

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.920
As spoilery as this could be I talked about
a white walker prophecy theory in a video.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.630
I’ll add a link for those that want to watch
it.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:22.630
It’s all about brokering a truce in the
name of balance. But a 
lot of the alliegences on the show right now

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.600
will shift and the people you think are heroes
might end up being villians.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.220
You can just watch that video for a much more
detailed breakdown.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:39.980
Question 5 - Johanna Adams asks can weirwood
trees be grown or transplanted?

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:44.630
Probably not transplanted but they can certainly
be grown. So you could plant and grow new

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:48.930
ones. But I don’t think they’re like the
ents in Lord of the Rings. The trees are connected

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.280
to a certain type of nature magic, but they’re
not going to just pick up and start running

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.010
around.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:58.080
We’ll learn more about them in winds of
winter and season 5.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:01.890
Question 6 - Brian Navarro asks does the Great
Other have sleeper cells around the world

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:08.890
and are there other people that worship 
the great other?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:20.210
I think it will look more like what you saw
during Aegon’s Conquest. He allowed people

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.670
to surrender or join his army.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:31.120
You start with your forces in the Lands of
Always Winter, then as they push south they

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:34.390
slowly kill people and turn them into wights
making their army stronger. Aegon allowed

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.210
people to surrender and join his army.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.390
Since we saw that white walker march past
Samwell in season 2 it’s possible that they

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.690
could leave people alone if they’re not
perceived to be a threat.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:45.240
So the further south the White Walkers push,
the larger their army grows.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.840
At a certain point I think we’ll see people
try to serve the true balance of nature and

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:53.280
if the forces of the red god are doing something
to thwart that people could take action against

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.030
them. But that doesn’t mean that they’d
be serving the White Walkers or the Great

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:56.570
Other.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:06:00.650
A really simple way to think of it would be
the enemy of my enemy is my friend. You could

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.960
start to see a lot of that.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.990
Question 7 - Tomo asks who’s storyline are
they going to cut out in season 5?

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:12.170
They’re not so much cutting storyline’s
out as they’re cutting characters out and

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:14.560
giving those stories to other characters.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:18.360
For example, we haven’t heard about any
Greyjoy Uncle castings, those people do a

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.460
few notable things in book 4. It’s possible
that they could give those parts of the story

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:26.620
to Theon’s sister, Yara. Her name in the
books is different than on the show. But you

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.530
get the idea.

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:34.530
The did the same thing with Gendry giving
him Edric Storm’s story and giving Hot Pie

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:36.510
Gendry’s story.

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:41.370
The big parts of the story stay close to the
books, the biggest changes are always the

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:46.430
characters themselves.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.630
Question 8 - VOD asks if you had to choose
a religion which one would you pick?

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:55.930
I do like me some resurrection but I’d probably
pick the Old Gods, just so I wouldn’t have

00:06:55.930 --> 00:07:00.200
to sit through long boring rituals or church
sermons like in the faith of the seven.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:04.760
A lot of times it feels like in the books,
people’s religions have a lot to do with

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:09.700
their personalities, like arya worships death
because she’s so hardcore. But before she

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.540
worshipped the old gods like her family.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:16.340
I feel like my personality changes year to
year just as much as some of the characters,

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.700
so the god I worship would probably change
over time too. But right now, I’ll keep

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.060
it simple and say a prayer at a heart tree
every once and a while.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:26.750
Question 9 - Virus asks, where is the Blackfish?
Where has he been since the Red Wedding?

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:33.750
This is a rare case when the show and the
books do the same thing. He escaped the Red

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:40.040
Wedding Massacre because he was outside the
castle when shit went down. He ran back to

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.570
Riverrun and has been holed up there since
then.

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:45.990
If you remember, Riverrun sits on a small
piece of land in a body of water. So when

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.540
he pulls the drawbridge up. The castle can
only be reached by boat. So they can’t just

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.550
march an army up to it’s gates.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.389
The show is changing what happens after that.
Based on the characters that they killed of

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:56.919
during the red wedding it seems like they’re
just going to cut the Blackfish out of the

00:07:56.919 --> 00:07:59.410
story unless he shows up in some other way.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.710
He has a pretty notable story in Book 4. But
again, they’re not doing that on the show.

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:08.889
In both cases, he ends up alive and on the
run. So he can always come back into the story

00:08:08.889 --> 00:08:09.199
in a future season.

00:08:09.199 --> 00:08:13.699
and Question 10 last one - Nicole Mott asks
do people get rez sickness when they get brought

00:08:13.699 --> 00:08:15.820
back to life? Reduced stats suck.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:20.860
I laughed a little when I saw this because
I used to be addicted to Warcraft. And yes,

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:23.360
there is a certain level of Rez Sickness and
reduced stats each time you get brought back.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.710
Beric Dondarrion on the show says that each
time R’hollor brings him back from the dead

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:30.620
it feels like a little piece of him gets left
behind. So presumably there is a limit to

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.550
the number of times someone can be brought
back.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:38.020
Or at a certain point you just become a mindless
soulless zombie.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:43.320
I know the show cut Lady Stoneheart out, but
so far she’s the furthest gone that we’ve

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:47.620
seen someone come back from. But I think she
was a special case due to the circumstances

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:53.890
of her death and the will of her mind.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.779
